note S5 scrub emit: a small unit whose output sha256 (s5.cases s5-scrub-emit) pins the exact scrub sequence:
note the n checks, the STP XZR loop, MOVZ #0 for the free pool registers (f has one parameter and one
note local below them), X16, X7, X18-X26, X29, then MOVI #0 for V0-V31. A dropped or retargeted zeroing
note word changes the output (s5-mutants.cases m-zpool, m-zvec, m-movz16).
om2
fn f n ulong to ulong
a = add n 5
k = scrub n
ret add a ulong k
end
fn main to int
r = f 32
ret int sub r 37
end
